AltoConvexCreditLineMarket::settleBadDebt(uint256)
├── when caller is not owner
│   └── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount before validating amount or burning tokens
├── when assets is zero
│   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput without changing state
├── when assets exceeds badDebtAssets
│   └── it should revert with an arithmetic panic before calling burn without changing state
├── when the market is active, frozen, or paused
│   └── it should remain available
├── when settling part of recorded bad debt
│   ├── it should burn assets directly from the owner without allowance or transfer
│   ├── it should reduce badDebtAssets by the burned amount
│   ├── it should emit BadDebtSettled
│   └── it should preserve active debt, positions, collateral, credit limit, claimable fees, and Convex state
├── when settling all recorded bad debt
│   └── it should reduce badDebtAssets to zero
├── when settlement restores unused credit capacity
│   └── it should permit new borrowing only up to the restored amount
└── when borrow token is DUSD
    ├── given the market is an authorized burner
    │   ├── it should burn DUSD directly from the owner without allowance
    │   ├── it should reduce DUSD total supply and the market minter bucket
    │   └── it should leave no DUSD in the market
    ├── given the market is not an authorized burner
    │   └── it should revert atomically
    ├── given DUSD is paused
    │   └── it should revert atomically
    └── given bad debt exceeds the market minter bucket because fees remain unclaimed
        ├── it should reject settlement above the minted bucket atomically
        └── it should allow settlement after fees are claimed and both recipients transfer their shares to the owner
